    [X] Support goto... but how?! We can find labels within functions,
        but how are we going to like... reproduce the Python callstack
        which is usually in place?!..
        E.g. in the following, if we `goto some_label`, we should then
        find ourselves inside a while loop. O_o

            while (1) {
                some_label: y = 4;
            }

        Or even here,

            {
                x = 1;
                some_label: y = 2;
                z = 3;
            }

        ...the 3 assignments are 3 ParseMatch children of the {...}.
        So how do we jump into the middle of the Python handler for that
        {...} (i.e. on_block__compound_statement)?..

        See also: minictests/goto.c

        [X] We could probably cheat at just support goto to labels within
