    [ ] For ({...}), see:
        https://gcc.gnu.org/onlinedocs/gcc/Statement-Exprs.html
        "The last thing in the compound statement should be an expression
        followed by a semicolon; the value of this subexpression serves as
        the value of the entire construct.
        (If you use some other kind of statement last within the braces,
        the construct has type void, and thus effectively no value.)"

[ ] Look at Yacc's implementation (or any papers on it), see what their
    approach is... backtracking?..

